+# Performance-Only RTL timing candidate r1
+
+Independent branch `ec-performance-only-rtl-timing-r1-20261115`, based on
+`42c9409c1abb275564c0b2f97a99f529a064a01f`. Functional lineage is the frozen
+`8491167d` snapshot followed by the explicitly authorized Performance-Only
+profile and existing CDC/DCache/SVB storage changes. This repository stores
+the frozen source snapshot as `0390a80`; it does not contain the original
+`8491167d` git object. BJL/Frontend/GH_FIFO sources were unchanged between
+`0390a80` and this candidate's parent.
+
+No full-shell implementation, FPGA operation, Native modification, controller
+change or signal to the other session's processes was performed. Small module
+jobs used CPUs 248–249, two Vivado threads and nice 19. They have finished.
+
+## Evidence and technical conclusion
+
+The historical failing 15 MHz report's worst setup path is inside **Xilinx DDR4
+calibration**, on `mmcm_clkout0` (3.332 ns):
+
+```
+design_1_i/ddr4_0/inst/u_ddr4_mem_intfc/u_ddr_cal_top/
+  u_ddr_cal/u_ddr_cal_addr_decode/ub_ready_reg/C
+    -> address initialization/calibration selection -> parity reduction ->
+  mcal_PAR_dly_reg[0][6]/D
+```
+
+Slack −3.457 ns; four LUT levels; data delay 6.657 ns = logic 0.492 ns + routing
+6.165 ns (92.609%). Two nets alone contribute 2.644 ns (`cal_ADR[23]`, fanout 5)
+and 2.372 ns (`cal_PAR_int6_i_4_n_0`, fanout 8); `ub_ready` has fanout 72 and
+0.962 ns routing. Physical sites are X118–123/Y66–76, all **SLR0, clock region
+X4Y1**, verified against the U280 device database. This is not a cross-SLR data
+path or a CDC path. The report came from an illegally routed implementation;
+its timing is diagnostic evidence, not a signoff result.
+
+RTL ownership chain in generated DDR IP:
+
+- `ddr4_v2_2_cal_addr_decode.sv:1179`: `ub_ready` write; :949–963 and :1975:
+  address generation.
+- `ddr4_v2_2_cal.sv:1522`: `ub_ready` selects microcontroller versus initialization
+  address. Synthesized hierarchy names are rebuilt and do not delimit the
+  original RTL module boundaries.
+- `ddr4_v2_2_cal_top.sv:814`: parity input transposition; :839–848: parity XOR;
+  :889–907: controller/calibration parity selection and first delay register.
+
+Native and current DDR IP have identical hashes for the three initially checked
+calibration source files and **all 138 configurable XCI parameters match**.
+Early C4 checkpoint source hashes match as well. Native routed DDR WNS/WHS is
++0.052/+0.010 ns; certified SVB component +0.023/+0.006 ns, both at 3.332 ns.
+There is no evidence that an EC Chisel edit inserted this DDR logic or changed
+its protocol. Density-induced detours are consistent with the evidence; an
+exact causal attribution to any individual EC edit has not been established.
+Do not change DDR RTL or relax its clock based on this failed route.
+
+The active other-session structure candidate's **post-place estimates** have
+DDR WNS +0.281 ns and WHS −0.145 ns. Its worst global setup is PCIe +0.114 ns;
+worst hold −0.725 ns is XDMA IRQ-to-PCIe MSI, under the existing setup-2/hold-1
+exception. These are not routed results. CLB occupancy is 97.78/94.93/99.13%;
+SLR links are only 10.26/12.36% used in aggregate. Level-5 congestion windows are
+dominated by DCache/SVB; BJL occupies part of the same neighborhood. Local
+CLB/routing pressure, not exhausted total SLL capacity, is the immediate issue.
+
+## Implemented RTL
+
+`chipyard/generators/rocket-chip/src/main/scala/guardiancouncil/GH_FIFO.scala`
+changes only `GH_FIFO_SC` payload storage:
+
+```
+RegInit(Vec(256, UInt(82.W)))
+    -> Mem(256, UInt(82.W)) + 256 resettable written bits
+```
+
+The read remains asynchronous in the same target cycle. Reset masks stale
+payloads, including invalid `peek_bits`; reset dominates a simultaneous write.
+Enqueue/full, commit, reserve, rollback/replay priority, empty bypass and every
+public output are retained. No new DUT register stage or target cycle is added.
+
+Netlist/source connection: physical `frontend/BJL/u_channel_bj_[0-1]/sptr_reg`
+and `sync_0_reg_BUFG` nets -> `rocket/Frontend.scala:109` ->
+`r/R_BJL.scala:146` -> `GH_FIFO.scala:275` resettable payload and :319 dynamic
+read. Full emitted target FIRRTL contains eight 82×256 queues. Current full
+physical fanout reports show 41,571–41,591 loads on the BJL reset nets and
+about 5,223 loads per low read-pointer bit. The BJL paths themselves have ample
+setup slack; they are a measured source of FF, MUX and control-routing pressure.
+
+Existing DCache/SVB/PacketSequenceBank changes were inspected but not modified
+again. The GHM LocalMemAsyncQueue change retains frozen Gray pointers,
+synchronizers, source/sink clocks and reset handshakes, with source-local data
+selection equivalent to the original narrow queue. The examined timing paths
+do not identify an EC pipeline/CDC wiring defect. This audit is not a new
+whole-checker equivalence certificate.
+
+## Real paired Vivado module measurements
+
+Vivado 2021.1, xcu280-fsvh2892-2L-e, actual complete 82×256 modules, same
+out-of-context synthesis/options and 100 ns comparison clock. These are target
+module measurements, not a threaded Golden Gate host/full-shell estimate.
+
+| Metric | Reference | Candidate |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| post-opt LUT | 6,033 | 963 |
+| post-opt FF | 21,016 | 286 |
+| post-opt LUTRAM (included in LUT) | 0 | 384 |
+| post-opt F7/F8 MUX | 2,788 / 1,312 | 8 / 4 |
+| BRAM / DSP / URAM | 0 / 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 / 0 |
+| routed LUT | 6,029 | 957 |
+| maximum reset fanout | 21,016 | 290 |
+| maximum read-pointer fanout | 5,264 | 410 |
+| internal reg-to-reg max data delay | 7.905 ns | 4.872 ns |
+| internal max path logic / routing | 0.742 / 7.163 ns | 0.631 / 4.241 ns |
+| internal max path levels | 6 | 5 |
+| internal minimum hold slack | +0.070 ns | +0.044 ns |
+| fully routed / routable nets | 22,907 / 22,907 | 854 / 854 |
+| routing errors | 0 | 0 |
+
+The module's external ports lack top-level partition-pin locations. Vivado
+reports RTSTAT-10/no-routable-loads warnings on external outputs, and I/O hold
+numbers are not signoff-quality. The timing comparison above deliberately uses
+**internal register/memory endpoints only**, extracted from the routed module
+checkpoints. It does not certify the full target or DDR/PCIe timing.
+
+The earlier Yosys screen differs substantially (including BRAM inference), so
+its estimates must not substitute for the Vivado numbers above. Do not add a
+per-module delta to the full shell, or assume an eight-queue/threading multiplier.
+
+## Validation
+
+- Scala/Chisel compile and actual generated RTL: passed.
+- All public outputs, including invalid payload, 131,073-cycle comparison:
+  passed. Coverage includes 21,307 full cycles, 16,632 empty, 3,607 rollback,
+  6,536 replay, 21 reset/write collisions and 32,652 simultaneous commit/enqueue.
+- Inductive refinement on the actual 82×256 emitted netlists: passed.
+  Relation `reference[i] == (written[i] ? memory[i] : 0)`; pointers identical.
+  All full-width payload cones are checked for lane independence and symmetry;
+  SAT proves every control/output/next-state equation. Separate arbitrary-state
+  reset-base proof establishes the relation. Removing one next-state mask fails.
+- Actual Golden Gate MCRAM host: 4,096 token comparisons passed, including
+  full/empty/commit/rollback/replay/reset. A deliberate mismatch fails at token
+  100. The test uses atomic input tokens and a verification-only output snapshot;
+  no register is added to DUT interfaces. The initial split-port harness exposed
+  unstable peeks; that failed harness is retained separately and is not a DUT
+  failure. Model multithreading is disabled in this module test; the actual full
+  system/threaded-host integration remains a required gate.
+
+## Constraint candidate and integration
+
+Current recovery `clock-normalized.xdc` uses `concat` in eight replayed PCIe
+clock-group commands. Vivado 2021.1 logs unsupported-XDC Critical Warnings.
+`host-clock-no-concat.tcl` preserves the exact existing groups but emits one
+`get_clocks -filter` union per group. It changes no period, CDC synchronizer,
+false-path membership or setup/hold exception. Eight exact original group pairs,
+literal brackets, unions and empty-group behavior pass offline Tcl checks.
+The two-FF Vivado 2021.1 experiment confirms the old `concat` command creates
+**no valid timing exceptions**, while the replacement creates both intended
+clock-group directions with unchanged periods. Inspecting `report_exceptions`
+is essential: an explicit `get_timing_paths -from/-to` query still returns a
+diagnostic path under a clock-group exception and is not an admission test.
+Full checkpoint replay must wait for the main CAD resource to be free. This is
+an independently prepared constraint candidate, not an edit to the controller.
+
+The highest-value next integration candidate is **existing CDC/DCache/SVB
+structural base + this BJL storage change**, with proper clock-group replay.
+It attacks actual FF/MUX/control-network pressure without modifying DDR IP or
+target latency. New full generated-host elaboration, threaded-token/system
+validation, DUT/full-shell area, placement and routing must be measured before
+claiming a shell resource delta, legal route, timing closure or usable bitstream.
+No full implementation was queued into the other session's controller.
+
+`run.py`, `formal.py`, `host.py`, `module_cad.py`, `module_paths.py`, `analyze.py`,
+`prepare_constraints.py` and `constraint_syntax.py` reproduce the bounded checks.
+Their input/output paths and source hashes are preserved in `results.json` and
+the sealed artifact directory. Do not rerun into an existing output directory.
diff --git a/candidates/rtl-timing-r1/Reference.scala b/candidates/rtl-timing-r1/Reference.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ce39788
--- /dev/null
+++ b/candidates/rtl-timing-r1/Reference.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+package freechips.rocketchip.guardiancouncil
+import chisel3._
+import chisel3.util._
+class GH_FIFO_SC_Reference(val params: FIFOParams) extends Module with HasFIFO_SC_IO {
+
+  private def inc(ptr: UInt): UInt =
+    Mux(ptr === (params.depth - 1).U, 0.U, ptr + 1.U)
+
+  private def dec(ptr: UInt): UInt = Mux(ptr === 0.U, (params.depth-1).U, ptr - 1.U)
+
+  private def dist(a: UInt, b: UInt): UInt = {
+    // distance from b to a in ring [0, depth)
+    val d = Wire(UInt((log2Ceil(params.depth) + 1).W))
+    d := Mux(a >= b, a - b, a + params.depth.U - b)
+    d(log2Ceil(params.depth)-1, 0) // max is depth-1 (we keep one slot empty)
+  }
+
+  val mem = RegInit(VecInit(Seq.fill(params.depth)(0.U(params.width.W))))
+
+  val wptr = RegInit(0.U(log2Ceil(params.depth).W))
+  val sptr = RegInit(0.U(log2Ceil(params.depth).W))
+  val cptr = RegInit(0.U(log2Ceil(params.depth).W))
+
+  // can_commit: there exists reserved entries (cptr != sptr)
+  io.can_commit := (cptr =/= sptr)
+
+  // full depends on committed pointer (so we never overwrite uncommitted region)
+  val cptr_after_commit = Mux(io.commit && io.can_commit, inc(cptr), cptr)
+  val wptr_next = inc(wptr)
+  io.full := (wptr_next === cptr_after_commit)
+
+  // allow enqueue if not full (considering same-cycle commit freeing space)
+  val do_enq = io.enq_valid && !io.full
+  when (do_enq) {
+    mem(wptr) := io.enq_bits
+    wptr := wptr_next
+  }
+
+  // rollback has highest priority for speculative pointer
+  when (io.rollback) {
+    sptr := cptr_after_commit // if commit also asserted, use the updated committed point
+  }.elsewhen(io.need_replay_1){
+    sptr := dec(sptr)
+  }
+  .otherwise {
+    // reserve (advance sptr) if peek_valid
+    when (io.reserve && ((sptr =/= wptr) || (do_enq && (sptr === wptr)))) {
+      sptr := inc(sptr)
+    }
+  }
+
+  // commit advances cptr
+  when (io.commit && io.can_commit) {
+    cptr := inc(cptr)
+  }
+
+  // peek_valid: there is data between sptr and wptr
+  val empty_spec = (sptr === wptr)
+  io.peek_valid := !empty_spec
+
+  // bypass: if empty_spec but we enqueue into the same slot this cycle, peek the incoming
+  val peek_raw = mem(sptr)
+  io.peek_bits := Mux(empty_spec && do_enq && (wptr === sptr), io.enq_bits, peek_raw)
+
+  // occupancy measured between cptr and wptr
+  val occ = dist(wptr, cptr)
+  io.num_content := occ
+
+  io.status_twoslots   := Mux(occ >= (params.depth.U - 2.U), 1.U, 0.U)
+  io.status_threeslots := Mux(occ >= (params.depth.U - 3.U), 1.U, 0.U)
+  io.high_watermark    := Mux(
+    if (params.depth > 100) (occ >= (params.depth.U - 20.U)) else false.B,
+    1.U, 0.U
+  )
+}
diff --git a/candidates/rtl-timing-r1/TestQueue.cc b/candidates/rtl-timing-r1/TestQueue.cc
